course: dictionary
lesson: 16038
title: Veteran
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: A veteran is a person who has served in the armed forces, often someone who fought in a war. «My grandad is a veteran who served in the army.» The word served tells you what he did, so a veteran is someone who was in the army, navy or air force.
explain: A veteran can also be someone who has done a job or activity for a long time and has lots of experience. «She is a veteran teacher with thirty years in school.» Here veteran does not mean a soldier. Thirty years tells you she is very experienced.
explain: Veteran can be an adjective too, meaning old and experienced, or very old for cars. «The veteran car still starts on cold mornings.» To choose the right meaning, read the words around it and ask: is it a person who fought, a person with lots of experience, or an old thing?
fact: A veteran is someone who has served in the armed forces, especially in a war.
fact: In the UK and Canada, veterans are remembered on Remembrance Day, 11 November.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, veterans are remembered on Anzac Day, 25 April.
fact: «Veteran» can also mean someone with a lot of experience, such as «a veteran player» in sport.
fact: A veteran car is a very old car, usually made many years ago.
exercise: «My grandad is a veteran who served in the army.» Who is a veteran in this sentence? | A car that has broken down | A shopkeeper who sells fruit | A young child who plays in the park | *Someone who served in the armed forces
exercise: «The veteran teacher knew every child in the school.» What does veteran mean here? | A brand new teacher | A teacher who is always late | *Someone with lots of experience | Someone who fought in a war
exercise: «The veteran car still starts on cold mornings.» What does veteran mean in this sentence? | Very fast | Painted bright red | *Very old | Brand new
test: «Veteran players can still teach the young team a lot.» What does veteran mean in «veteran players»? | Players who never win | Players who have just joined the team | Players who are very young | *Players who have lots of experience
test: In Australia and New Zealand, on which day are veterans remembered? | Veterans Day | *Anzac Day | Remembrance Day | Christmas Day
exam: «He is a veteran of many wars.» What does veteran mean here? | A person who is new to a job | A person who plays music | *A person who has served in war | A person who lives in a cold country
